# macos.rb/CHANGELOG

## 20261108

0.50.1: ~ MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock: /peristent_app_paths/persistent_app_paths/, the misspelt name kept as an alias.

1. /MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock.peristent_app_paths/MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock.persistent_app_paths/
2. + MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock.peristent_app_paths, an alias of persistent_app_paths, so as callers of 0.50.0's name go on working.
3. ~ MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock.read: calls persistent_app_paths.
4. + test/MacOS/Defaults/ComAppleDock_test.rb: both names give the persistent apps' paths.
5. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.50.0/0.50.1/

## 20261107

0.50.0: The first release as a gem: + gemspec, tests in place of each library's self-run section, README, TODO and ROADMAP.md.

1. + macos.rb.gemspec: macos.rb, for Ruby 2.7 on, depending on CFPropertyList and plist.
2. + Gemfile, Rakefile.
3. + LICENSE: MIT, 2013 to 2026.
4. + README.md, TODO, ROADMAP.md.
5. + test/helper.rb, test/MacOS_test.rb, test/VERSION_test.rb, test/gemspec_test.rb, test/commands_test.rb for the command each library sends, and a test for each library under test/MacOS.
6. + test/fixtures: the output each library reads, in the form airport, defaults, df, diskutil, dscl, ifconfig, networksetup, say and system_profiler give it, with every MAC address, IP address and name made anonymous.
7. - the self-run section of lib/MacOS/Apple80211.rb, Applications.rb, Defaults.rb, Defaults/NSGlobalDomain/NSUserKeyEquivalents.rb, Dmg.rb, HardwarePort.rb, IfConfig.rb, Keychain.rb, SystemProfiler.rb, USBFlashDrive.rb, Users.rb and Voice.rb, the tests taking their place.
8. ~ lib/MacOS/Apple80211.rb, Keychain.rb, USBFlashDrive.rb: The header's first line names the file, in place of #!/usr/bin/env ruby, which only the self-run section needed.
9. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.11/0.50.0/

0.49.11: ~ MacOS::Apple80211: Where airport -I gives nothing, as from macOS 14.4 on, the attributes come from system_profiler SPAirPortDataType.

1. ~ MacOS::Apple80211.attributes: airport -I's, or where it gives none, the current network's from system_profiler SPAirPortDataType, with its Channel and Security as channel and link auth too, and its name as SSID where macOS doesn't redact it.
2. + MacOS::Apple80211.system_profiler_airport
3. + MacOS::Apple80211.airport_attributes, private: airport -I's attributes, as .attributes read them before, less the WARNING line printed in their place from macOS 14.4 on.
4. + MacOS::Apple80211.system_profiler_attributes, private.
5. ~ MacOS::Apple80211.airport_i: '' where airport isn't there, rather than an Errno::ENOENT.
6. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.10/0.49.11/

0.49.10: ~ lib/MacOS/VPN.rb: The header's second line names MacOS::VPN, rather than repeating the file's name.

1. ~ lib/MacOS/VPN.rb: /# MacOS\/VPN.rb/# MacOS::VPN/ in the header's second line.
2. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.9/0.49.10/

0.49.9: ~ MacOS::DiskUtil.free_bytes_for_device_id, .free_bytes_for_volume_name: The bytes available, as an Integer, rather than the 512-byte blocks used, as a String.

1. ~ MacOS::DiskUtil.free_bytes_for_device_id, .free_bytes_for_volume_name: `df -k`, in place of `df`, and its Available column times 1024, in place of its Used column.
2. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.8/0.49.9/

0.49.8: + require 'yaml' in MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock and MacOS::Defaults::NSGlobalDomain::NSUserKeyEquivalents, and require 'set' in the latter, so as each works loaded on its own.

1. ~ lib/MacOS/Defaults/ComAppleDock.rb: + require 'yaml'. Loaded without lib/MacOS/Defaults.rb, ComAppleDock.to_yaml raised a NameError.
2. ~ lib/MacOS/Defaults/NSGlobalDomain/NSUserKeyEquivalents.rb: + require 'set', 'yaml'. Loaded on its own, NSUserKeyEquivalents.to_yaml raised a NameError, and .read_keys did on Rubies before 3.2.
3. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.7/0.49.8/

0.49.7: ~ MacOS::SystemProfiler: Its aliases work on the module, and boot_mode gives the boot mode rather than the boot volume.

1. ~ MacOS::SystemProfiler: + module_function for every alias, from boot_volume_string to time_since_boot. alias_method makes instance methods alone, so MacOS::SystemProfiler.computer_name and the rest raised a NoMethodError.
2. ~ MacOS::SystemProfiler.boot_mode, .boot_mode_string: Aliases of boot_mode_data, in place of boot_volume_data.
3. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.6/0.49.7/

0.49.6: ~ MacOS::Keychain.wifi_password: nil where the keychain has no password for the network, rather than a NoMethodError.

1. ~ MacOS::Keychain.wifi_password: stderr[/password: "(.+)"/, 1], in place of stderr.match(/password: "(.+)"/)[1], which called [] on nil when nothing matched.
2. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.5/0.49.6/

0.49.5: ~ MacOS::LaunchControl: An instance holds the plist it's made with, and unloads it.

1. ~ MacOS::LaunchControl#initialize: /init/initialize/. As init, new(path_to_plist) raised an ArgumentError and new left the path unset.
2. ~ MacOS::LaunchControl#unload: path_to_plist defaults to the instance's own, as #load uses.
3. ~ MacOS::LaunchControl.load, .unload: The plist's path escaped for the shell, so as a path with a space in it is one argument; + require 'shellwords'.
4. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.4/0.49.5/

0.49.4: ~ MacOS::Defaults: Every domain, rather than one; a Defaults for each, rather than an ArgumentError; and from_yaml writes what to_yaml wrote.

1. ~ MacOS::Defaults.domains: `defaults domains`.chomp.split(', '), in place of .split('\n'), which split on a backslash and an n. defaults domains gives every domain on one line, separated by commas.
2. ~ MacOS::Defaults.all, .bulk_export_to_plist_files, .bulk_import_from_plist_files, .from_yaml: new(domain: domain), in place of new(domain), initialize taking domain: only.
3. ~ MacOS::Defaults.from_yaml: DEFAULT_YAML_FILENAME, in place of DEFAULT_YAML_FILE, which isn't defined.
4. ~ MacOS::Defaults#from_yaml: + attributes, the list of single key: value pairs to_yaml writes for the domain, each written with defaults write; true where every write succeeds. It read an attributes it was never given.
5. ~ MacOS::Defaults.from_yaml: Each domain's attributes passed on to #from_yaml.
6. + MacOS::Defaults#defaults_arguments, private: a value as defaults write takes it, with -bool, -int, -float, -array, -dict or -string as its type.
7. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.3/0.49.4/

0.49.3: Core Ruby in place of the extension libraries other than Version, each of which patched a core class of any program loading macos.rb.

1. ~ MacOS::Applications.start: system('open', path, exception: true), in place of Kernel.run.
2. ~ MacOS::Applications: alias_method for launch, open and run, in place of alias_methods; - require 'Kernel/run', 'Module/alias_methods'.
3. ~ MacOS::Dmg: alias_method for filename, dmg_filename and image_name, and their writers, in place of alias_methods; - require 'Array/all_but_last', which nothing used, and 'Module/alias_methods'.
4. ~ MacOS::HardwarePort.parse: line.match(...)&.captures, in place of line.captures(...); - require 'Thoran/String/Captures/captures'.
5. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: line[..., 1] and line.match(...)&.captures, in place of line.capture and line.captures.
6. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.all_matching: Regexp.union(pattern), in place of pattern.to_regexp; a String is still matched literally.
7. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.bring_down_interface, .destroy_interface: system(..., exception: true), in place of run.
8. ~ lib/MacOS/IfConfig.rb: - require 'Kernel/run', 'Regexp/to_regexp', 'String/to_regexp', 'Thoran/String/Capture/capture', 'Thoran/String/Captures/captures'.
9. ~ MacOS::SystemProfiler: + .field, private, giving a field's value with system_profiler_output[/<name>: (?<value>.+)$/, :value], in place of grep and split in each of the nine; split[1] and split[3], in place of second and fourth; - require 'Ordinal/Array', 'String/grep'.
10. ~ MacOS::Defaults::NSGlobalDomain::NSUserKeyEquivalents.read_keys: plist_dict.lines.grep(/=/), in place of String#grep; - require 'String/grep'.
11. - lib/Kernel/run.rb: Kernel#run 0.3.1
12. - lib/Regexp/to_regexp.rb: Regexp#to_regexp 0.0.0
13. - lib/String/grep.rb: String#grep 0.2.0
14. - lib/String/to_regexp.rb: String#to_regexp 0.3.0
15. - lib/Thoran/String/Captures/captures.rb: Thoran::String::Captures#captures 0.3.0
16. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.2/0.49.3/

0.49.2: ~ MacOS::USBFlashDrive.all_mount_points: Every mount point, rather than the first.

1. ~ MacOS::USBFlashDrive.all_mount_points: stdout.scan(/Mount Point: (.+)$/).flatten, in place of stdout.captures(/Mount Point: (.+)$/), which gives the groups of the first match only.
2. ~ lib/MacOS/USBFlashDrive.rb: - require 'Thoran/String/Captures/captures', which nothing in it uses now.
3. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.1/0.49.2/

0.49.1: ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: Each call starts afresh, and reads its lines with or without a trailing space; MacOS::IfConfig.output is private again.

1. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: ifconfigs and ifconfig are locals, in place of @ifconfigs and @ifconfig on the class. @ifconfig was never reset, so every call after the first began with the previous call's last interface, and returned it twice.
2. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: - the unused local interface.
3. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: Output with no interfaces gives [], rather than [nil].
4. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: / *ether (.+?) ?$/, in place of / *ether (.+) $/. ifconfig no longer ends these lines with a space, so no interface had a MAC address.
5. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.parse: / *inet (\d+(?:\.\d+){3}) netmask (.+?) ?$/, in place of one ending (.+) $/. Nor does it end an inet line without a broadcast address with one, so loopback had no IPv4 address.
6. ~ MacOS::IfConfig.output: private, as it was until IfConfig 0.6.1 commented the line out.
7. ~ MacOS::VERSION: /0.49.0/0.49.1/

0.49.0: + lib/MacOS/VERSION.rb; - each file's own date, version and changes from its header; + CHANGELOG.

1. + lib/MacOS/VERSION.rb: MacOS::VERSION, the library's version.
2. ~ lib/MacOS.rb: + require 'MacOS/VERSION'
3. ~ lib/MacOS.rb and every file under lib/MacOS: - the date and version lines and the changes noted since the last version, the library's version and the CHANGELOG taking their place.
4. + CHANGELOG: an entry for every version from 0.0.0, each what its commit says.

0.48.0: MacOS 0.1.0: Require every library; + MacOS.version, in place of lib/MacOS/Version.rb.

1. + require 'MacOS/Apple80211', 'MacOS/Applications', 'MacOS/Defaults/ComAppleDock', 'MacOS/Defaults/NSGlobalDomain/NSUserKeyEquivalents', 'MacOS/DiskUtil', 'MacOS/Keychain', 'MacOS/USBFlashDrive', 'MacOS/Users', 'MacOS/Voice' and 'MacOS/VPN'.
2. - require 'MacOS/Version'
3. + MacOS.version, taken from lib/MacOS/Version.rb 0.1.0.
4. - lib/MacOS/Version.rb, and with it MacOS::VERSION::STRING, which MacOS.version.to_s gives.

0.47.2: /module Defaults/class Defaults/ for ComAppleDock and NSUserKeyEquivalents, so as they load beside MacOS::Defaults, which is a class.

1. ~ MacOS::Defaults::ComAppleDock 0.5.3: /module Defaults/class Defaults/
2. ~ MacOS::Defaults::NSGlobalDomain::NSUserKeyEquivalents 0.2.1: /module Defaults/class Defaults/

0.47.1: MacOS::Voice 0.0.1: Quote say's ?; read names with spaces in them whole; - the newline at the end of each description.

1. ~ all(): say -v '?', the shell otherwise matching ? against one-character filenames.
2. ~ new_from_line(): A name with spaces in it, as Bad News, is read whole, rather than its first word being taken as the name and its second as the localisation.
3. ~ new_from_line(): - the newline at the end of the description.

0.47.0: MacOS::Voice 0.0.0: + MacOS::Voice: the voices say knows, each with its name, localisation and description, and a random one, taken from Kernel/say.rb 0.4.2.

1. ~ lib/Kernel/run.rb: Kernel#run /0.3.0/0.3.1/


